STATUS: Generate one desktop landing-page concept screenshot for the Android
game Urkaaaz, using the attached game screen and repository artwork as visual
references. This is a website design concept only, not a playable web game or
website implementation.

## What to attach

Attach these references when running the prompt:

1. **Required — the campaign-screen screenshot supplied by the user.** Use it
   as the primary reference for the game's actual world, chapter presentation,
   and in-game visual language. Show it as a clearly framed gameplay preview;
   do not flatten the full screenshot into the website background.
2. **Recommended — `assets_src/dashboard/dashboard_background_approved.png`.**
   Use it as a source of approved character art and color mood for the hero
   section. Do not copy its Dashboard controls into the website.
3. **Recommended — the historical standalone game logo
   `urkaaz-logo-main-menu.png`
   from the session Library.** It was recovered from Git history; its former
   repository path was `android-app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/logo_main_menu.png`.
   Use this artwork as the exact game logo; do not replace it with the AFACODE
   publisher mark.
4. **Recommended — `assets_src/campaign/chapter-maps/campaign_chapter_01_green_frontier_map.png`.**
   Use it for a secondary campaign/world preview if that section is visible.
5. **Optional — `assets_src/splash/splash_background.png`.** Use it only as an
   additional environment and lighting reference, not as a full-page backdrop.
6. **Optional — `assets_src/splash/afacode_company_logo.png`.** Place it as a
   small publisher mark in the footer only. It is the publisher logo, not the
   Urkaaaz game logo.
7. **Optional — one real match-screen screenshot.** Attach a current gameplay
   capture if the page should show combat in addition to the campaign view.
   Do not invent gameplay content when no match screenshot is attached.

The standalone game logo existed on the legacy Start screen and was removed
from the current repository. Attach the recovered `urkaaz-logo-main-menu.png`
from the Library and use that artwork in the website header. Pair it with the
`CATAPULT CHAOS` subtitle only if it is not already part of the attached logo.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG concept screenshot:
  `urkaaaz_website_landing_page_concept.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/website/screen-concepts/`.
- Canvas: exactly 1920 × 1080 pixels, landscape 16:9.
- Show one complete desktop website viewport edge-to-edge. Do not add a browser
  window, device frame, alternate screen, presentation mockup, or annotations.
- The result is a static visual concept. Do not generate HTML, CSS, JavaScript,
  or production website assets.

## Page concept

- Design a polished promotional landing page for **Urkaaaz! Catapult Chaos**,
  an Android fantasy siege strategy game.
- Use concise English copy throughout this concept.
- Create a clear top navigation with the live-text wordmark, a few short
  section links (for example `GAMEPLAY`, `CAMPAIGN`, `FEATURES`), and one
  restrained call to action.
- Make the hero the visual focus: bold game title and one short, readable
  tagline on one side, with the supplied campaign or match screenshot shown
  as the actual in-game preview on the other. Keep the game screenshot
  rectangular and legible; do not stretch, repaint, or convert it into a
  decorative background.
- Below the hero, show a compact preview of the core game pillars using no
  more than three content cards: catapult aiming, deploying units and spells,
  and progressing through campaign chapters. Use the attached map/art assets
  when available.
- Finish with a simple footer. If the AFACODE logo is attached, use it only as
  a small publisher attribution.

## Art direction

- Extend Urkaaaz's existing painterly fantasy style into a clean, premium
  landing page: deep forest greens, charcoal stone, dark timber, warm
  parchment, and restrained antique-gold accents.
- Use dramatic but readable contrast. Keep parchment panels and gold trim as
  accents rather than turning the whole page into a campaign screen.
- Give the title and game preview generous space. The page should feel like a
  real desktop game website, not a collage of Android UI panels.
- Use consistent alignment, spacing, and typography. Keep navigation, hero
  content, cards, and footer clearly separated without excessive decoration.
- Use only artwork present in the supplied references. Do not invent new
  characters, bosses, biomes, logos, or gameplay scenes.

## Copy and factual limits

- Keep all text short, correctly spelled, and readable at the full screenshot
  size. Avoid lorem ipsum and decorative pseudo-text.
- Suitable button copy: `EXPLORE THE CAMPAIGN` or `SEE GAMEPLAY`.
- Do not invent a release date, price, user count, review score, awards,
  supported platforms beyond Android, online multiplayer, or a store URL.
- Do not draw a Google Play badge or imply that a store listing already exists.
- Do not add signup forms, purchases, login, social feeds, or features not
  evidenced by the references.

## Separation from the Android game

- This is a public promotional website concept, not a new game screen.
- Do not copy the full Dashboard, Loadout, Match HUD, campaign selector, or
  status bars as the website layout. Use supplied in-game screenshots only as
  embedded product previews.
- Do not add fake app controls that appear to operate the game.
- Keep any publisher attribution visually separate from the Urkaaaz title.

## Review checklist

- Confirm the image is one complete 1920 × 1080 desktop website viewport.
- Confirm the hero uses the exact title `URKAAAZ! Catapult Chaos` and the
  attached game art/screenshots retain their proportions and visible content.
- Confirm the overall visual language matches Urkaaaz without copying an
  entire game screen as the webpage.
- Confirm no unsupported release, store, rating, audience, or multiplayer
  claims appear.
- Confirm the page has clear hierarchy and restrained, readable copy.
- Do not treat this concept image as a production website or import it into
  the Android app.

## Negative prompt

mobile app screen, game HUD, flattened campaign map, fake gameplay scene,
invented characters, invented boss, invented biome, browser chrome, phone
mockup, device frame, multiple screenshots, collage, code editor, HTML, CSS,
JavaScript, fake Google Play badge, fake store URL, release date, price,
ratings, awards, user counts, multiplayer claim, login form, checkout,
newsletter form, lorem ipsum, gibberish text, misspelled game title,
AFACODE used as the game logo, cluttered navigation, tiny unreadable copy,
excessive parchment, ornate gold overload, watermark, signature
